config-connector-extensions patch 0024: mockgcp lists and undeletes service accounts, and names them by unique ID.

For resourcemanager.gcp.hfl.dev ProjectDefaultServiceAccounts, which
finds a project's default service accounts with serviceAccounts.list and
acts on them by unique ID, as Terraform's
google_project_default_service_accounts does. Written here, in
mockiam/serviceaccounts.go: ListServiceAccounts (one page, deleted
accounts left out); DeleteServiceAccount keeps the account under
projects/{p}/deletedServiceAccounts/{uniqueId}; UndeleteServiceAccount
restores it, by unique ID only, and fails if an account with its email
exists again; delete, disable and enable take a unique ID as well as an
email (GetServiceAccount already did), and a unique ID finds only
accounts that are not deleted. Deleted accounts are kept for ever (the
API keeps them 30 days).
Upstream candidate: yes.

